      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Between Wilmington and Lewes, Smyrna was the most important port, shipping grain, lumber, tanbark, and produce northward.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smyrna%2C_Delaware",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Duck Creek Village Historic Area preserves Delaware’s earliest communities with homes, churches, and cemeteries along the creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://unearththevoyage.com/delaware-smyrna-authentic-historic-attractions/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Nearly 500 historic buildings line Smyrna’s streets, many earning spots on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://unearththevoyage.com/delaware-smyrna-authentic-historic-attractions/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Smyrna Museum Complex showcases the town’s development from earliest settlement days through curated exhibits and local narratives.",
